{"strongs": "H4419", "word": "מַלָּח", "translit": "mal.lach", "root": "מלח", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "mariner", "definition": "[ מַלָּח ] noun masculine mariner (loan-word from Assyrian mala—u Dl HWB 412 compare Id Prov 1 .178 ; Hal ZA iv. 1880, 53 ; so also Aramaic (see Brock .), whence Arabic Frä 221 ); — plural מַלָּחִים Jonah 1:5 ; Ezek 27:29 מַלָּחַיִךְ Ezek 27:27 מַלָּחֵיהֶם v Ezek 27:9 ( Ba NB 49 Anm. 3 ); — mariners, sailors of ship going to Tarshish Jonah 1:5 (compare רַב הַחֹבֵל v Jonah 1:6 ); to Tyre Ezek 27:9 , compare v Ezek 27:27 v Ezek 27:29 (|| חֹבְלִים ). מִלְחָמָה see I. לחם .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4664')\">BDB4664</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H4419')\">H4419</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4663')\">BDB4663</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4665')\">BDB4665</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>מַלָּח</bdbheb>] <b>noun masculine</b> <highlightword>mariner</highlightword> (loan-word from Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>mala—u</highlight></transliteration> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dl')\">Dl<sup>HWB 412</sup></lookup> compare Id<sup><ref ref=\"Prov 1\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"200\" onclick=\"bcv(20,1,1)\">Prov 1</ref>.178</sup>; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Hal')\">Hal<sup>ZA iv. 1880, 53</sup></lookup>; so also Aramaic <placeholder2993/> (see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Brock')\">Brock</lookup>.), whence Arabic <placeholder2994/> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Frä')\">Frä<sup>221</sup></lookup>); — plural <bdbheb>מַלָּחִים</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Jonah 1:5\" b=\"32\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(32,1,5)\">Jonah 1:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 27:29\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(26,27,29)\">Ezek 27:29</ref> <bdbheb>מַלָּחַיִךְ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 27:27\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"27\" vBegin=\"27\" cEnd=\"27\" vEnd=\"27\" onclick=\"bcv(26,27,27)\">Ezek 27:27